WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.166
[music]

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.066
[Instructor] Cool. So we've got
some background music

3
00:00:08.066 --> 00:00:11.700
playing in our game [happy game music]
for our nice happy forest,

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.033
and our nice happy character
jumping through the Scene.

5
00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.700
So, one of the last things
that we're going to do

6
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.133
is we're going to add in some
"Sound Effects" for the Player.

7
00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:29.933
Now Sound Effects are a bit
different than using Music Audio

8
00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:32.366
because we actually need
to trigger those Sound Effects

9
00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:35.233
in our code. So actually,
what we're going to do is,

10
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:37.566
first we're going to go
into our PlayerController Script,

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.100
and now in our PlayerController Script,

12
00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:44.533
we're going to create
two new variables.

13
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.400
So the first one will be a public,

14
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:52.800
and in this case,
since we're actually using Audio clips,

15
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.766
we can actually just use
the "AudioClip".

16
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.666
So now we have an AudioClip class.

17
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.100
And we'll call this,
The "jumpSound."

18
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:12.100
And then we need a second
AudioClip for our "crashSound."

19
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.133
So now that we have
these public variables,

20
00:01:24.866 --> 00:01:26.866
now if we go back into Unity,

21
00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:29.600
you can see when we click
on the Player,

22
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.933
so there's the Jump Sound
which has no Audio Clip,

23
00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:34.933
and the Crash Sound 
which also has no Audio Clip.

24
00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:37.933
So we're actually going to go
into the "SFX."

25
00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:41.733
So there's a bunch of different
options for jumping and crashing.

26
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:45.666
So if we just make sure
that we go back to the Player,

27
00:01:45.666 --> 00:01:50.500
and we'll just drag one of them.
I'll just do crash2 for our crash sound.

28
00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:54.200
And then jump3 for our jump sound.

29
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.466
So now what you're going to do is,
in your PlayerController class,

30
00:01:58.466 --> 00:02:00.900
you're going to create
two new variables yourself

31
00:02:01.566 --> 00:02:03.433
for the AudioClips.

32
00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:05.600
One AudioClip variable for the jump,

33
00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:09.400
and one for the crash, 
and make sure that they're public,

34
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.533
so that way we can assign it,
when we get into Unity.

35
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.266
And then in Unity, you're going to click
the Player,

36
00:02:17.933 --> 00:02:21.533
and then just make sure that you go
into your Course Library, Sound,

37
00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.133
SFX for Sound Effects.

38
00:02:24.566 --> 00:02:27.666
Drag and drop one of the jumps
into the jump sound,

39
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:29.666
and one of the crashes 
into the crash sound.

40
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.466
Now it's your turn.

41
00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:35.700
[music]
